WEBVTT

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:29.900
Good morning.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:30.910
Morning.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.440
Good morning, San-chan.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.050
Great weather today.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.150
San-chan!

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.370
Kinda weather that makes you wanna go out.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.330
Have you been eating aside from lunch?

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.420
Sure is.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:39.050
Yes.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.770
You always look so sickly, 
it's got me worried.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:46.090
I know! I'll bring you some 
nori next chance I get.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:48.310
Doesn't get much more 
nutritious than Saga's nori!

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:49.910
Thank you.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.710
Well, good morning everyone!

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:58.820
Good morning.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:03.050
We've got a fine view of 
Imari Bay again today,

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:05.070
and the horseshoe crabs are looking lively.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:10.150
I'm hoping you'll all cook, slice, 
and dry with the kinda pride

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:13.300
folks working for the only dried 
squid maker in Kyushu ought to have.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.650
Time for the company anthem!

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:18.460
Leading us today is gonna be Tatsumi-kun.

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:20.700
If you could!

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:21.230
Right!

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:35.570
<b><i>Zombie Land Saga 
Revenge</i></b>

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:35.440
<i>The more you chew, the more flavor you get!</i>

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.580
<i>And when you think there can't be 
more, you still get more flavor!</i>

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:45.580
<i>That's what makes you really shine, 
and shine is just what you do!</i>

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:49.550
<i>Leaving your hometown</i>

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:52.580
<i>Oh-so far behind</i>

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:59.330
<i>Heading on a journey, prepared to be eaten</i>

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:02.970
<i>The spirit of squid!</i>

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:06.740
<i>Will not be wasted on me!</i>

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:13.650
<i>But the truth is, you couldn't 
have expected you'd be eaten one day</i>

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:17.700
<i>They may say you're dried now</i>

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.310
<i>But I will never forget your tears</i>

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:24.170
<i>Even though there should be 
no way a squid could cry</i>

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:28.120
<i>No, there shouldn't be at all!</i>

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.660
<i>Cook it, pull it, dice it, 
and dry it up now!</i>

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:34.840
<i>Cook it, pull it, dice it, 
and dry it up now!</i>

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.260
<i>The spirit of squid!</i>

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:41.840
<i>Will not be wasted on me!</i>

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:45.300
<i>I love the dried squid</i>

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:55.330
<i>From the Kojima Food Factory!</i>

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:02.950
I'm back.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:04.530
There you are!

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:05.990
Welcome back, Ai-chan.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:07.280
Welcome home.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:08.500
I brought you guys something.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:09.480
Tono-sama dried squid.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:10.170
Yay!

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:14.740
Tae-chan! Cut that out!

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:16.250
We're all gonna share that!

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:17.330
Enough!

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.830
Hey, Ai. The water's yours if you want it.

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:21.630
Thanks. I think I will.

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:26.880
I'm glad nobody found out 
we're zombies today!

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.180
It's been surprisingly easy 
to keep it under wraps.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.590
And we've all been working for a month now.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:34.140
Should be fine as long as 
nothing crazy happens.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.860
It's you two I'm worried about, Sakura.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:39.550
I'll be careful.

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:41.350
Tae-chan, manners!

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.720
If you think about it,

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:47.770
Yugiri probably needs to be most careful 
since she has a service job...

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:49.490
But I don't think we need to worry.

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:51.670
She really took to it easily!

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:54.050
Like she already had the right bearing.

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:57.050
Tae-chan, stop!

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:58.870
If we keep working, we should be 
able to get out of debt eventually!

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.990
Cut it out! No—

00:03:58.870 --> 00:03:59.650
Yeah!

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.210
<i>The girls of Franchouchou, in the 
last winter of the Heisei era,</i>

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.970
<i>pulled off a show at Arpino 
with a 500-member audience.</i>

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.980
<b>Franchouchou's Miracle Performance 
on a Snowy Evening</b>

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.970
<i>After that, our profile 
blew up like a balloon,</i>

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:14.600
<i>with our first CD selling like hotcakes!</i>

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:18.790
<i>It was such a thrill to get to 
perform at a bunch of new venues!</i>

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:20.370
<i>Then a month later...</i>

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:23.740
<b>Concert</b>

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:21.300
And boom!

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:26.840
We're barreling right into a show at the 
Ekimae Fudosan Stadium... EFS for short!

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:29.660
And then, once you've got the crowd on fire,

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:33.250
you'll blow them up with the new 
song as an encore, like boom!

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:39.000
Franchouchou's legend is going to 
keep blowing up like a cluster bomb!

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.470
<b>Ekimae Fudosan Stadium</b>

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:42.500
<i>So, Franchouchou was on 
stage for a show at the EFS!</i>

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:43.480
<i>And the result?</i>

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.050
<i>We managed to sell 500 tickets 
of the 30,000-person venue.</i>

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:52.440
<i>That's an attendance rate of 1.66%!</i>

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:53.730
<b>Attendance Rate</b>

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:54.630
<i>We bombed in the worst way 
any idol group can imagine!</i>

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:54.640
<b>BOMBED</b>

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.730
<i>Our performance was totally shaky,</i>

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:59.230
<i>which meant no encore, and our new 
song was put back on the shelf...</i>

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:02.840
<i>Plus, we ended up saddled with a huge debt!</i>

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:04.650
<i>A-boo-hoo-hoo!</i>

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.450
Is this hell?

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:10.780
<b>Franchouchou falls 
apart at EFS</b>

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:17.940
<i>We might've had a huge disaster, 
but we still want to get on stage again!</i>

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:22.690
<i>That's why we've all gotten jobs
 to pay off that debt!</i>

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:24.820
<i>We're not gonna give up!</i>

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:30.330
<i>As for our producer, Kotaro-san...</i>

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:30.550
<b>Jofuku's
 Retreat</b>

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:34.420
Pope's nose...!

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:36.380
Pope's nose! Why would you...

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:37.490
Why call it that?!

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.000
Oh, you want me to save Saga?

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.360
Gee, I wonder...

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.510
Hell no! It ain't happening!

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:45.200
Saga's doomed!

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.930
It's the Sagapocalypse!

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:53.070
That's... That's why I 
wanted to take Saga and...

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.690
Pope's nose!

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:58.290
Good grief! What must that feel like?!

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.360
Hey, Saga!

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:04.960
Time for your milk!

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:09.680
Come on, hold still!

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.680
We keep trying, but it 
never turns out right...

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:17.520
It just doesn't have the lively look,
 y'know what I mean?

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.600
Well, we are dead, after all.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.930
I think Kotaro-san is the only one 
who can get the color right...

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:26.710
What the hell is wrong with Shades, anyway?

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:30.360
<b>One step at a time</b>

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:30.360
<b>Return show!</b>

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:30.360
<b>Get ready!</b>

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:30.360
<b>Idols in 
progress</b>

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:30.360
<b>Anniversary of 
our first show!</b>

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:30.360
<b>We're all magical!</b>

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:30.360
<b>You get stronger
 from every failure!</b>

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:29.980
I'll go check on him again.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:32.990
Good evening.

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:34.650
Is he in?

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:43.470
Kotaro-san! Wake up!

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:45.210
Kotaro-san?

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:48.810
What the...?! So dark! I can't see a thing!

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:51.310
That's because you grew 
your hair out too long!

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.890
Oh, it's Sakura. Again.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:57.110
It can't be healthy to act like this.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:59.300
Oh, and listen to this!

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.000
We all worked hard and managed to get

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:03.340
more money together for this 
month than we expected!

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:11.740
Kotaro-san... what happened 
at the EFS was a real shame,

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:17.130
but I think, in the end,
 it'll be a good experience for us!

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:19.550
If we can get past this, 
I know we'll be even—

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:21.260
It's already over.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:22.380
We're not letting it end!

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:26.330
I don't know when,
 but we'll pay off that debt!

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:30.520
No matter how long it takes,
 we'll do our best and keep working!

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:34.130
Just go, okay?

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:39.190
We've got a death metal show at Geil's soon.

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:41.570
That was where we went on 
stage for the first time.

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:46.010
We all decided to perform there again 
so Franchouchou could get a fresh start.

00:07:46.410 --> 00:07:51.020
We wanna sing the song we 
didn't get to at the EFS.

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:54.010
So, please, come and see us.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:05.820
What's with you?! Huh?!

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:08.190
You're all squinched up, like a pope's nose!

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:09.670
The chicken, I mean! Huh?!

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:12.790
Hey, Sakura, say, "I'm a pope's nose!"

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:14.230
Overhead toss!

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:18.660
How can we get the old Kotaro-san back?

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:22.180
Being a total wreck for a 
whole month is pretty bad.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:28.470
It's going to be hard for Franchouchou 
to operate without Tatsumi-san.

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:30.520
I'm just guessing here, but...

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:33.640
It might not be about the money.

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:37.280
You suppose there's something 
that he wouldn't tell us?

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:40.250
When you get down to it, 
it was weird that he wanted us

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:42.860
to perform at the EFS 
when he did in the first place.

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:46.240
Now that you mention it, I can't imagine 
why he thought it'd be a success...

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:48.770
Maybe he was... in a hurry, or something?

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:49.640
For what?

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:51.250
I dunno, but...

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:53.920
If Ai-han's on the right track

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:55.630
and we can figure out the details,

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.850
there may be a way to get through to him.

00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:01.800
I wonder if we could find 
anything in Tatsumi's room.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:10.040
It's open.

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:11.690
Hell yeah!

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:13.940
All right, time for a raid!

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:14.940
Yay!

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:16.710
H-H-Hang on a sec!

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:17.950
Hey, hey, hey, check it out!

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:29.180
Nobody break anything, okay?

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.640
Ow, ow, ow...

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:37.550
Oh, what do I do now?!

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:43.820
<i>Yeah, yeah, yeah, like this!</i>

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:47.520
<i>Yeah, yeah, yeah, like this!</i>

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:50.300
<i>Yeah, yeah woohoo— 
Wait, no, not like this...</i>

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:50.310
<i>Encore</i>

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.010
This is the song we were supposed 
to sing for the encore.

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:52.810
<i>It's not "yeah, yeah, woohoo."</i>

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:54.080
<i>It's more like...</i>

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:55.190
Guess it's a work-in-progress tape.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.130
<i>Yeah, yeah....</i>

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:58.300
<i>Yeah, yeah, yeah!</i>

00:09:58.300 --> 00:09:59.660
<i>Yeah, okay...</i>

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:02.610
<i>Yeah, yeah, yeah, like this!</i>

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:05.980
This must be his usual process.

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:08.160
You can feel the passion.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:10.420
Before he burned out, anyway.

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:15.760
We never figured out why 
he was in a rush, either.

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:20.180
But now we know how he felt 
about the EFS show...

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:24.380
Let's make sure Kotaro-san 
comes to our next one.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:30.090
If we can sing the encore we didn't before, 
maybe he'll turn back to normal.

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:33.100
If he feels better, maybe we'll understand!

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:36.240
That might be the most effective way.

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:40.120
No other way about it. We're gonna 
hit him where it feels good!

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:42.410
Yeah!

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:08.930
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:13.940
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:13.940
<b>Snacks!</b>

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:16.150
Here you are.

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:21.560
Reporting in after another day 
defending order in Saga!

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:26.510
The drinks you pour me after 
days like these taste so sweet!

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:30.840
I'm hoping you continue to 
take good care of Saga.

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:35.250
Of course! I'll be here 
to see you every night!

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:38.210
Those eyes... makes me wanna arrest 'em!

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.790
Never been here before!

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:47.450
Wrong bar.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:56.650
<b>Bar
Chinatsu</b>

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:07.720
Kotaro-han...

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:10.060
You're drinking too much.

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:11.820
Wrong...

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:13.150
Excuse me?

00:12:13.590 --> 00:12:15.300
I was wrong...

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:18.540
I was wrong...

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:21.120
I was so wrong...

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:29.220
Okay, if we can pull that off
 on stage, we'll be good to go.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:30.670
No reason we can't!

00:12:31.990 --> 00:12:33.640
That just leaves Kotaro-san...

00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:38.120
We never heard from him, huh?

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:41.370
After what Yugiri-san told us 
about how he was last night...

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:44.790
He was coming apart at the seams.

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:46.780
I don't want any of you to worry.

00:12:47.110 --> 00:12:49.610
I'm gonna go bring him in.

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:51.490
The rest of you should get ready!

00:12:52.990 --> 00:12:54.840
The show is tonight.

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:00.220
Please, hear me out!

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:02.960
I already told you to do whatever you want.

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:04.830
I'm only asking you to show up!

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:10.690
Me and the others want to sing 
your songs a whole lot more!

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:12.550
We want to keep being idols!

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:17.720
There is nothing more I can do.

00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:24.240
What happened to you?

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:26.900
Do you remember what you said?

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:29.570
I have what it takes!

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:32.230
I will never abandon you!

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:35.080
Where did that Kotaro-san go?

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:39.370
Guess I had less than I thought...

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:44.080
You're such a jerk! I don't care anymore!

00:13:58.300 --> 00:14:03.860
We're going to have to make this show 
a success, even without Kotaro-san.

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:14.100
We don't come around for a while and now 
the whole club's filled with new folks.

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:16.690
I hope Franchouchou is gonna be okay.

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:20.510
This is a heck of a spot to play 
after what happened at the EFS...

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:23.240
Just goes to show how important 
this show's gonna be.

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:25.780
Which means all we gotta do is support them!

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:26.220
True enough!

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:33.380
Idols?

00:14:33.380 --> 00:14:34.180
What the hell?

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:35.900
Franchouchou!

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:37.990
We've been waiting!

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:40.890
Are these chicks for real?

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:42.780
Come on, get on with it!

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:43.790
What's their deal?

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:47.490
Hey, we're Franchouchou!

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:51.930
Uh, a little while back, we 
tried to do a show at the EFS

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:54.740
and, well, we couldn't let it end like that!

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.200
So, next time, we're gonna pull it off!

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:59.710
Today is gonna be our 
first step towards that.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:02.460
We're gonna give you our best shot!
 Thanks for coming!

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:14.570
We've done a lot of shows this size before.

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:17.350
We'll pull this one off and get 
over what happened at the EFS!

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:24.040
It'll be okay... It'll be okay.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:34.050
How long are you going to darken 
my bar with that sorry look?

00:15:34.520 --> 00:15:37.400
Do you serve the customers
 verbal abuse here?

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:41.250
My real customers don't sleep here 
because they're scared of going home.

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:45.790
You said you were done, right? With this...

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:48.960
Genkai Zombie Energy Park Project of yours.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:51.300
It's called the Zombie Land Saga Project.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:52.320
Yeah, that.

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:58.090
It was a crazy scheme in the 
first place... Zombies as idols?

00:15:58.880 --> 00:16:01.960
I'm sure your Saga-ettes 
will get over it, too.

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:05.680
They'll look back on their undeaths 
and think of it as a fun memory.

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:07.940
The group name is "Franchouchou."

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:11.780
They'll be able to go on and 
have normal lives as zombies.

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:14.690
Well, technically they're not ali—

00:16:13.770 --> 00:16:16.770
There's a hard deadline on this project!

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.530
After making the biggest 
screwup any idol group could

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:22.540
and getting stuck with massive debt...

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:25.680
Even you should know that
there won't be enough time

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:26.960
to pull it off.

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:29.140
Please.

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:33.450
You've already demanded more than 
is reasonable of those girls,

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:35.710
and they managed to pull it off.

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:40.280
So, if you say it can't be done...

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:42.460
Well, it probably can't, then.

00:16:43.090 --> 00:16:46.290
This whole thing started 
because of what you wanted.

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:48.980
Why not let it end when you want?

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:54.200
Go on and tell them,
 "I've got no faith in the Saga-ettes."

00:16:54.210 --> 00:16:57.930
"You Saga-ettes are all washed up."

00:17:06.390 --> 00:17:08.730
It's not the Saga-ettes...

00:17:10.220 --> 00:17:11.370
It's Franchouchou!

00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:22.470
Yeah, that.

00:17:58.270 --> 00:18:01.470
<i>This is bad. It's gonna have 
the opposite effect...</i>

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:03.930
Y'all done yet? Then get off the stage!

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:06.090
We've still got another song left!

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:08.680
Sing it somewhere else, then!

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:12.350
You gals done or what?

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:13.730
What should we do?

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:15.400
We're not backing off after coming this far!

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:18.110
But... in this atmosphere...

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:19.020
Damn it.

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:21.320
Sakura...

00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:26.990
<i>No... after we all got on stage again...</i>

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:29.690
<i>It can't end like this...</i>

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:37.260
Kotaro-san!

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:40.430
Encore!

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:46.650
Encore! Encore! Encore!

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:50.480
Encore! Encore!

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:49.180
Who the hell are you?

00:18:49.180 --> 00:18:50.480
Shut up!

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:52.500
Come on, folks! All together now!

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:54.930
Encore! En—

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:54.930
I said shut it!

00:18:55.630 --> 00:18:56.450
Kotaro-san!

00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:00.530
Wow, that didn't hurt!

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:04.400
Encore! Encore!

00:19:03.630 --> 00:19:04.400
Enough!

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:06.800
Encore...!

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:12.790
Encore! Encore! Encore!

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:13.230
Quit screwing around!

00:19:17.410 --> 00:19:18.640
Damn you—

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:22.270
Been a while since we got into it!

00:19:22.270 --> 00:19:24.010
Let's kick some ass!

00:19:24.190 --> 00:19:26.960
Bring it on, then!

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:33.460
Gimme ten seconds with these clowns...

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:34.380
Saki-chan!

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:36.310
What do you think you're doing?!

00:19:36.740 --> 00:19:39.070
You're idols, so sing!

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:40.100
Be heard!

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:45.040
Let me hear the first cry as you're reborn!

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:46.920
Kotaro-san...

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:49.570
Sing!

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:54.290
Let's sing, everyone.

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:56.220
Let's sing!

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:57.490
There goes the kick!

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:02.910
Music, start!

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:36.750
<i>There's no turning back the clock, 
just facing what's happened</i>

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:39.890
<i>Take those past glories 
and just leave them be</i>

00:20:39.890 --> 00:20:41.560
<i>Just hang on tight</i>

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:43.870
<i>Never give up again</i>

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:47.050
<i>If you wanna make sure 
your loss has meaning</i>

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:48.080
<i>Get on your feet</i>

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:48.800
<i>Shake yourself off</i>

00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:50.430
<i>No matter how battered you are</i>

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:52.190
<i>After swallowing the pain</i>

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:54.350
<i>Could you stand up again?</i>

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:58.240
<i>Why worry about when to give up?</i>

00:20:58.240 --> 00:21:01.620
<i>Do you really want to go out on a whimper?</i>

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:03.500
<i>Bet on a comeback</i>

00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:04.880
<i>No matter how many times you fall</i>

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:06.890
<i>Take deferred and stockpiled dreams</i>

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:10.490
<i>And shout them out!</i>

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:18.960
<i>Even if it's a fight with no chance to win</i>

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:22.760
<i>That doesn't change the dream 
or how bad you want it!</i>

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:23.780
<i>Atone for</i>

00:21:23.780 --> 00:21:24.720
<i>your surrender</i>

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:25.580
<i>Retract your</i>

00:21:25.580 --> 00:21:26.460
<i>retreat and</i>

00:21:26.460 --> 00:21:27.320
<i>plan for</i>

00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:28.180
<i>the revolution</i>

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:29.050
<i>Rejoin and</i>

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:30.050
<i>start again</i>

00:21:30.050 --> 00:21:30.880
<i>The disappointment</i>

00:21:30.880 --> 00:21:31.780
<i>of failure,</i>

00:21:31.780 --> 00:21:32.690
<i>the mistakes</i>

00:21:32.690 --> 00:21:33.540
<i>and regrets,</i>

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:38.470
<i>can all be thrown into the fire 
that signals the new start!</i>

00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:45.600
<i>Even if the whole world gives up on you, 
keep fighting as long as you breathe!</i>

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:46.870
<i>The will</i>

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:47.860
<i>and the passion</i>

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:48.620
<i>To return</i>

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:49.590
<i>and fight back</i>

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:56.960
<i>Are what you need to shine 
bright and blaze on!</i>

00:22:20.500 --> 00:22:26.220
Awesome!

00:22:32.740 --> 00:22:35.150
That had to be the worst 
show I've ever been in.

00:22:35.150 --> 00:22:37.850
Could you even really call it a concert?

00:22:37.850 --> 00:22:40.060
Eh, close enough, right?

00:22:40.060 --> 00:22:41.090
Not even.

00:22:41.090 --> 00:22:44.090
Still, I wouldn't say it's far 
from what we're known for.

00:22:44.090 --> 00:22:45.350
No doubt.

00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:49.000
Sakura!

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:51.410
S-Sorry! I wasn't listening!

00:22:51.410 --> 00:22:53.630
Damn it, girl. You wanna die?

00:23:10.450 --> 00:23:15.980
Good morning, everyone!

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:21.920
<b>Episode 1</b>

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:21.920
<b>Good Morning Returns SAGA</b>

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:24.920
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:25.800
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:26.550
Sakura here!

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:27.260
<b>TV Report</b>

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:28.420
Things are as crazy as ever around here,

00:23:27.380 --> 00:23:28.010
<b>White Ryu</b>

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:30.460
but being able to sing together 
again makes me so happy!

00:23:30.460 --> 00:23:32.590
We're gonna make this revenge happen!

00:23:32.590 --> 00:23:35.090
Next time on <i>Zombie Land
Saga Revenge</i> Episode 2:

00:23:35.090 --> 00:23:36.940
"The SAGA of an Almost-Broken Radio."

00:23:35.350 --> 00:23:37.470
<b>Episode 2: The SAGA of an Almost-Broken Radio</b>

00:23:36.940 --> 00:23:37.960
Be sure to watch!
